markdown <<MARKDOWN
<!-- Pitfall 3 -->
<div style="max-width:1000px; margin:0 auto; font-family:ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial; background:#FFFFFF; padding:32px; color:#292F36; line-height:1.6; font-size:16px;">
<div style="border-radius:18px; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(41,47,54,0.08); border:1px solid #e3e6ea;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; padding:26px;">
<div style="color:#FFFFFF; font-size:26px; font-weight:800;">Pitfall 3: Trusting Confident-Sounding Answers Too Much</div>
</div>
<div style="background:#F4F6F8; padding:36px;">
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap:32px;">
<div>
<div style="border:1px solid #dfe3e8; border-radius:18px; padding:24px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(41,47,54,0.04);">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:14px; color:#0093A4;">Scenario</div>
<div style="margin-bottom:18px;">Dr. Patel, an assistant principal, asks AI to summarize a newly released district grading policy before a staff meeting.</div>
<div style="background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px; margin-bottom:18px;">
<div style="font-size:16px">Summarize this newly released district grading policy for me to share with staff.</div>
</div>
<div>The summary states that late work can no longer receive full credit under any circumstances. The language is clear and decisive, so Dr. Patel shares it with the faculty. Later, a teacher points out that the policy actually allows exceptions at teacher discretion. The incorrect summary causes frustration and a follow-up email clarifying the mistake.</div>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<div style="border:1px solid #dfe3e8; border-radius:18px; padding:24px; margin-bottom:24px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(41,47,54,0.04);">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:12px; color:#ED6060;">The Pitfall</div>
<div>Mistaking clear, authoritative language for correctness.</div>
</div>
<div style="border:1px solid #dfe3e8; border-radius:18px; padding:24px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(41,47,54,0.04);">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:12px; color:#0093A4;">Quick Tip</div>
<div style="margin-bottom:18px;">Confidence in tone does not equal accuracy — always compare AI summaries directly to original documents.</div>
<div style="background:#F7F8FA; border-left:5px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:14px; padding:18px;">
<div style="font-size:16px">Summarize this policy in bullet points and include 3 direct quotes (with section headings) that support each key claim. Also list any sections that are ambiguous or allow exceptions.</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:32px;">
<details style="border:1px solid #dfe3e8; border-radius:18px; background:#FFFFFF; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(41,47,54,0.04);">
<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:20px; font-weight:800; font-size:20px; color:#0093A4;">What’s Going on Under the Hood</summary>
<div style="padding:0 20px 20px 20px; border-top:1px solid #F4F6F8;">The AI is optimized to sound helpful and confident, not cautious. It doesn’t internally track uncertainty or flag ambiguous interpretations. If a confident tone is statistically common in similar documents, the model will reproduce it — even when the interpretation is incomplete or wrong.</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
MARKDOWN
